  "raw_text": "205\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nKulki Kaikanka 13:32\n):\n \nBaha tasbaya yang nani sâbi\n \nkaiki banhri ba naku sa:…\n \n–\n \nThat land that we spied is like\n\nthis:…\n \n/ Esa tierra que espiamos es así:…)\n\nSadiusi\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nSadducee\n \n/ Saduceo\n\nSahwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto multiply, to propagate, to become plentiful, to become abundant, to become numerous\n \n/ multiplicar,\npropagar, ser abundante, ser numeroso\n\nSahwi banhkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto multiply and fill\n \n/ multiplicar y llenar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nbh29\n):\n \nsahwi tasba na bangkbia\n \n–\n \nto multiply and fill the earth\n \n/ multiplicar y llenar la tierra)\n\nSai\n \n(\ndict,dictu,db\n) (adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \ndark, something black, something dark\n \n/ oscuro, algo negro, algo oscuro\n\nDaiwan taya saika dadingkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ntanner\n \n/ curtidor\n\nSaika\n \n(\ntkl\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npassword\n \n/ contraseña\n\n(Construct:\n \nSaiki, Saikam\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: Not commonly used / No se usa comúnmente)\n\nSaikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nSaiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto make dark, to tan\n \n/ oscurecer, broncearse\n\nS\na\nîka\n \n(\nSa\nika)\n \n(construct form of /\n \nforma constructiva de:\n \nS\nî\nka\n)\n \n–\n \nmedicine, remedy, drug, bait\n \n/ medicina, remedio, droga,\n\ncebo (usado\n \npara pescar)\n\nTairi sa\nî\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmosquito repellent\n \n/ repelente de mosquitos\n, repelente de zancudos\n\nSail\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsail\n \n/ vela\n\nSailar\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu\n;\n \nSaila\n-\ndictu-alt\n;\n \nSela\n-\ndictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsailor\n \n/ marinero\n\nSaiman lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsimony\n \n/ simonía\n\nSain\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmiracle, sign\n \n/ milagro, señal\n\nAisa sainka smalkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncircumcision teaching\n \n/ enseñanza de la circuncisión\n\nAisa sainka daukaia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nto circumcise\n \n/ circuncidar\n\nSain\n \nbîla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsign\n \nlanguage\n \n/ lenguaje de señas\n\nSain daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto perform a miracle\n, to perform a sign\n, to make a sign (communicating in signs or sign\n\nlanguage\n)\n \n/ realizar un milagro, realizar un s\ne\nñ\nal\n, hacer un s\ne\nñ\na\n \n(comunicarse en s\ne\nñ\nas\n \no lenguaje de s\ne\nñ\nas\n)\n\nSain\n \nmunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sign (a document), to make a signal\n \n/ firmar (un documento), hacer una señ\na\n\nTnata yua nani sainka ba\n \n–\n \nthe sign of the last days\n \n/\n \nla señal de los\n \nú\nltimos d\ní\nas\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ntkl\n):\n \nGâd Kingka lâka sturka yamni smalkanka ba tnata yua nani\n \nsainka markka tânka tara bri ba kum sa\n \n–\n\nThe preaching of the good news is an important feature of the sign of the last days\n \n/ La predicación de las buenas\n\nnoticias del Reino de Dios es una característica importante de la señal de los\n \nú\nltimos d\ní\nas\n)\n\nSait\n \n–\n \nside\n, aside\n \n/\n \ncostado, a un\n \nlado\n\nSait\n \nra\n \n(\na/\nt:\n \nSaitra\n)\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nto the side, going to the side,\n \ngoing to the\n \nside\n \nprivately\n, outside of\n, separate from\n \n/\n \nal\n\nlado, yendo hacia un lado, yendo hacia un lado en privado, fuera de, separado de\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\njl1\n)\n:\n \nWitin nani ba rug lâka ba wina sait ra sa\n \n–\n \nThey are aside (separate) from immorality\n \n/ Ellos est\ná\nn aparte\n\n(separados) de la inmoralidad\n)\n\nSait ra kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be set aside, to be put to the side, to be separate from\n \n/ ser puesto a un lado, ser\nseparado de\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-10/20\n):\n \nDîa muni yawan gridi l\nȃ\nka bara aidul l\nȃ\nka wina sait ra kaia sa?\n \n–\n \nWhy must greediness and\nidolatry be put to the side (rejected)?\n \n/ ¿Por qué la codicia y la idolatría deben dejarse de lado (rechazarse)?)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlv53\n):\n \nTasba na wina saitra kaia tnatka wala …\n \n–\n \nAnother way to be separate from this world …\n \n/ Otra\nmanera de estar separado de este mundo ...)\n\nSaiwaia\n \n(\nv\n-\nintrans\n;\n \ntrans:\n \nSaikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto become dark\n \n/\n \nponerse\n \noscuro\n, oscurecerse, anochecer\n\nSaiwan\n \n(adj, v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado\n)\n \n–\n \ndark, darkened, became dark\n \n/ oscuro, oscurecido, se volvió\n \no\nscuro\n\nSaiwan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndusk, evening\n \n/ anochecer, tarde\n\nSaiwan yamni\n \n(a greeting / un saludo)\n \n–\n \nGood dusk/evening\n \n(a greeting said around the time between 5\nand 7 pm) / Buen anochecer/ Buenas tarde (un saludo entre las 5 y las 7 de la tarde)\n\nSakahkaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSkahkaia\n\nSakaia\n \n(sometimes / a veces:\n \nSâkaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take out, to open, to extract, to pull out, to take away, to produce, to bear,\nto find, to get, to draw, to remove\n \n/ sacar, abrir, extraer, arrancar, llevarse, producir, soportar, aguantar, encontrar,\nconseguir, deducir, quitar\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \nFrom Spanish verb\n \n/ Del ve\nrbo español: Sacar\n)\n\nAihka aihka sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \nseparate, to scatter\n \n/ apartar, separar, esparcir",
